WEBVTT

00:00:01.705 --> 00:00:29.142
Great Expectations by Charles Dickens Copyright Black Cat Publishing Charles Dickens I am Charles Dickens.

00:00:29.202 --> 00:00:32.071
I am a famous writer.

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:36.172
Do you know the names of some of my books?

00:00:36.232 --> 00:00:44.650
Oliver Twist, David Copperfield, A Tale of Two Cities, Great Expectations?

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:48.134
Victoria is the Queen.

00:00:48.194 --> 00:00:52.788
England is a very important country in my time.

00:00:52.848 --> 00:00:59.601
It has a lot of power in the world, from Europe to India and China.

00:00:59.661 --> 00:01:04.080
But there are a lot of poor people in England.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:08.622
The rich ladies and gentlemen don't care about them.

00:01:08.682 --> 00:01:11.894
But I am sorry for the poor people.

00:01:11.954 --> 00:01:15.025
That is why I write my stories.

00:01:15.085 --> 00:01:19.566
I want to show that money is not important.

00:01:19.626 --> 00:01:24.669
In my story, Pip is a good boy when he is poor.

00:01:24.729 --> 00:01:30.658
But when he is a gentleman, he is cold and unkind.

00:01:30.718 --> 00:01:34.186
It isn't good to think about money.

00:01:34.246 --> 00:01:37.908
It is better to think about people.

00:01:37.968 --> 00:01:40.568
Read my story.

00:01:40.628 --> 00:01:44.800
Do you agree?

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:48.912
Part 1.

00:01:48.972 --> 00:01:52.434
The prisoner on the marshes.

00:01:52.494 --> 00:01:55.505
Pip is a young boy.

00:01:55.565 --> 00:01:58.012
He has no mother and father.

00:01:58.072 --> 00:02:03.019
He lives on the marshes near the Great River Thames.

00:02:03.079 --> 00:02:06.810
One day he is sitting in the churchyard.

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:10.220
He is looking at his parents' graves.

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:13.451
Suddenly, someone grabs him.

00:02:13.511 --> 00:02:15.422
It's a prisoner.

00:02:15.482 --> 00:02:19.362
He is escaping from the prison ships on the river.

00:02:19.422 --> 00:02:22.473
Pip is very afraid.

00:02:22.533 --> 00:02:24.434
What's your name?

00:02:24.494 --> 00:02:26.076
Pip, sir.

00:02:26.136 --> 00:02:28.408
I want food.

00:02:28.468 --> 00:02:29.858
Get me some.

00:02:29.918 --> 00:02:30.838
Yes, sir.

00:02:30.898 --> 00:02:32.749
You must be very hungry, sir.

00:02:32.809 --> 00:02:34.450
Yes, I am.

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:38.602
And bring me a file to cut these chains.

00:02:38.662 --> 00:02:41.432
But don't tell anyone.

00:02:41.492 --> 00:02:43.073
No, sir.

00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:46.294
Pip runs back to the house.

00:02:46.354 --> 00:02:50.626
He lives with his sister and her husband, Joe.

00:02:50.686 --> 00:02:53.757
They are poor, simple people.

00:02:53.817 --> 00:02:56.196
Joe is the village blacksmith.

00:02:56.255 --> 00:02:58.324
And he is very kind.

00:02:58.384 --> 00:03:00.436
He loves Pip.

00:03:00.496 --> 00:03:05.109
But Pip's sister is nasty and bad-tempered.

00:03:05.168 --> 00:03:08.581
She likes hitting her little brother.

00:03:08.641 --> 00:03:15.406
In the middle of the night, Pip steals some food from the kitchen for the prisoner.

00:03:15.466 --> 00:03:19.058
You are a bad boy.

00:03:19.118 --> 00:03:21.540
Get me some food.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:26.321
I'm afraid of my sister, but I'm very afraid of the prisoner.

00:03:26.381 --> 00:03:31.052
It's very bad to steal food, but I must do it.

00:03:31.112 --> 00:03:33.463
Where is Joe's file?

00:03:33.523 --> 00:03:36.354
I must take it to help the prisoner.

00:03:36.414 --> 00:03:40.635
Pip gets up early and runs across the marshes.

00:03:40.695 --> 00:03:43.416
It is very cold and misty.

00:03:43.476 --> 00:03:46.206
The sun is rising.

00:03:46.266 --> 00:03:51.603
He sees another prisoner, but the man runs away.

00:03:51.663 --> 00:03:57.172
Pip takes the food and the file to the prisoner in the churchyard.

00:03:57.231 --> 00:03:58.963
Here is the food.

00:03:59.023 --> 00:04:02.146
You must be very cold and hungry, sir.

00:04:02.206 --> 00:04:03.987
Thank you, boy.

00:04:04.047 --> 00:04:06.128
This food is good.

00:04:06.188 --> 00:04:09.531
There's another prisoner on the marshes, sir.

00:04:09.591 --> 00:04:11.983
He has a scar on his face.

00:04:12.043 --> 00:04:12.974
What?

00:04:13.033 --> 00:04:15.016
He is my enemy.

00:04:15.076 --> 00:04:16.687
Give me the file.

00:04:16.746 --> 00:04:19.679
Quick, I must find him.

00:04:19.739 --> 00:04:22.632
Pip goes back to the house.

00:04:22.692 --> 00:04:28.236
When his sister cannot find the food for dinner, she is very angry.

00:04:28.296 --> 00:04:31.346
But then some soldiers arrive.

00:04:31.406 --> 00:04:33.828
They want Joe to help them.

00:04:33.888 --> 00:04:36.489
He must mend their equipment.

00:04:36.549 --> 00:04:39.980
The soldiers are looking for the prisoners.

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:43.992
Joe takes Pip to the marshes to watch.

00:04:44.052 --> 00:04:46.984
The soldiers find the prisoners.

00:04:47.044 --> 00:04:49.894
They are fighting because they are enemies.

00:04:49.954 --> 00:04:54.484
The soldiers take the prisoners back to the prison ship.

00:04:54.544 --> 00:04:56.534
I'm afraid.

00:04:56.594 --> 00:04:59.875
The prisoner thinks that I'm helping the soldiers.

00:04:59.935 --> 00:05:01.376
It isn't true.

00:05:01.436 --> 00:05:04.977
The soldiers are taking the prisoners to the prison ship.

00:05:05.037 --> 00:05:08.278
Poor men, I'm sorry for them.

00:05:08.338 --> 00:05:11.059
You are my enemy.

00:05:11.119 --> 00:05:13.390
I want to kill you.

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:15.230
You're stupid.

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:20.864
Now we're both going back to prison.

00:05:20.924 --> 00:05:25.308
Part 2.

00:05:25.368 --> 00:05:33.526
Miss Havisham A strange old lady lives in a big house in the village.

00:05:33.586 --> 00:05:36.300
Her name is Miss Havisham.

00:05:36.359 --> 00:05:41.184
One day, she asks Pip's uncle to send Pip to her.

00:05:41.244 --> 00:05:43.808
She wants to see a child.

00:05:43.868 --> 00:05:48.860
His sister says, Miss Havisham is very rich.

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:51.501
You must be polite, Pip.

00:05:51.561 --> 00:05:55.624
Perhaps she wants to give you a lot of money.

00:05:55.684 --> 00:05:57.325
Good luck, Pip.

00:05:57.385 --> 00:05:58.496
Be careful.

00:05:58.556 --> 00:06:02.298
Some people say Miss Havisham is mad.

00:06:02.358 --> 00:06:06.691
Uncle Pumblechuck takes Pip to her house.

00:06:06.751 --> 00:06:09.893
Its name is Satis House.

00:06:09.952 --> 00:06:14.156
A beautiful young girl opens the gate for Pip.

00:06:14.215 --> 00:06:17.271
She is very proud.

00:06:17.331 --> 00:06:19.606
Come in, boy.

00:06:19.666 --> 00:06:22.238
Miss Havisham wants to see you.

00:06:22.297 --> 00:06:24.700
But I don't like you.

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:28.762
Your boots are dirty and your hands are rough.

00:06:28.822 --> 00:06:31.304
Is Miss Havisham your mother?

00:06:31.364 --> 00:06:32.774
No.

00:06:32.834 --> 00:06:35.536
I have no mother or father.

00:06:35.596 --> 00:06:40.330
But I live with Miss Havisham and she gives me everything.

00:06:40.390 --> 00:06:44.102
But don't ask questions, boy.

00:06:44.162 --> 00:06:48.614
Miss Havisham is sitting in a dark room.

00:06:48.674 --> 00:06:52.103
She is wearing an old wedding dress.

00:06:52.163 --> 00:06:53.884
It isn't white.

00:06:53.944 --> 00:06:57.285
It's yellow because it's very old.

00:06:57.344 --> 00:07:02.336
There are a lot of clocks, but they aren't working.

00:07:02.396 --> 00:07:05.687
They all say the same time.

00:07:05.747 --> 00:07:08.378
Twenty to nine.

00:07:08.438 --> 00:07:11.279
Hello, Pip.

00:07:11.339 --> 00:07:15.436
Well, Estella, do you like Pip?

00:07:15.496 --> 00:07:18.475
No, he isn't a gentleman.

00:07:18.535 --> 00:07:21.348
He's a blacksmith's boy.

00:07:21.407 --> 00:07:25.410
And Pip, do you like Estella?

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:27.892
She's very beautiful.

00:07:27.952 --> 00:07:31.955
Pip thinks you're beautiful, Estella.

00:07:32.015 --> 00:07:35.768
So break his heart.

00:07:35.828 --> 00:07:41.333
Pip visits Miss Havisham and Estella many times.

00:07:41.392 --> 00:07:44.024
Sometimes they play cards.

00:07:44.084 --> 00:07:46.367
Sometimes they sing.

00:07:46.426 --> 00:07:50.220
But Estella is always proud.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:55.924
Pip begins to love her, but she doesn't love him.

00:07:55.984 --> 00:08:01.078
One day, Miss Havisham takes him into a special room.

00:08:01.138 --> 00:08:06.772
There is a long table with a very old wedding cake on it.

00:08:06.832 --> 00:08:12.132
Spiders and mice and rats are everywhere.

00:08:12.192 --> 00:08:16.071
Today is my birthday, Pip.

00:08:16.131 --> 00:08:19.342
Push me around the table.

00:08:19.402 --> 00:08:25.183
This is my wedding cake from a long time ago.

00:08:25.243 --> 00:08:27.774
But where is her husband?

00:08:27.834 --> 00:08:30.414
I hate men.

00:08:30.474 --> 00:08:35.226
I am teaching a stellar to hate men too, Pip.

00:08:35.285 --> 00:08:37.734
You're only a boy.

00:08:37.795 --> 00:08:43.407
But when you are a man, you must leave Satis House forever.

00:08:43.467 --> 00:08:45.678
But I want to marry Estella.

00:08:45.738 --> 00:08:49.902
Silly boy, I hate you.

00:08:49.962 --> 00:08:55.196
One day, Pip meets another boy in the garden.

00:08:55.256 --> 00:08:56.777
They fight.

00:08:56.837 --> 00:09:03.442
The boy boxes like a gentleman, but Pip wins because he fights like a blacksmith.

00:09:03.502 --> 00:09:07.728
Estella is watching the fight.

00:09:07.788 --> 00:09:11.124
You're the winner.

00:09:11.184 --> 00:09:13.636
Well done, Pip.

00:09:13.696 --> 00:09:16.718
You may kiss me if you like.

00:09:16.778 --> 00:09:20.822
Pip kisses Estella on the cheek.

00:09:20.882 --> 00:09:24.974
Later, Miss Havisham says goodbye to him.

00:09:25.034 --> 00:09:28.358
This is the last time, Pip.

00:09:28.418 --> 00:09:31.640
I don't want to see you again.

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:34.042
Here is some money.

00:09:34.102 --> 00:09:37.276
You must be a blacksmith.

00:09:37.336 --> 00:09:40.419
But I want to see Estella again.

00:09:40.479 --> 00:09:42.240
I love her.

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:45.800
I am sending Estella to Paris.

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:49.071
I am making her a lady.

00:09:49.131 --> 00:09:52.632
But you are a blacksmith, Pip.

00:09:52.692 --> 00:09:58.832
You must work with Joe Godgeri.

00:09:58.892 --> 00:10:05.744
Great expectations and Kent.

00:10:05.804 --> 00:10:08.692
Rochester.

00:10:08.752 --> 00:10:15.454
Rochester is a historic city in Kent, near London.

00:10:15.514 --> 00:10:21.788
It has a very old cathedral and a Norman castle.

00:10:21.848 --> 00:10:27.151
The castle is almost a thousand years old.

00:10:27.211 --> 00:10:31.444
Dickens was in Rochester a lot.

00:10:31.504 --> 00:10:37.513
His house, Gad's Hill Place, is near Rochester.

00:10:37.573 --> 00:10:47.972
There is a Dickens Museum in Rochester and a Dickens Festival every summer and every Christmas.

00:10:48.032 --> 00:10:54.625
Great Expectations takes place in Kent and London.

00:10:54.685 --> 00:10:58.976
Joe's Forge is near Rochester.

00:10:59.036 --> 00:11:03.961
The coach to London goes from Rochester.

00:11:04.021 --> 00:11:10.206
There is a house in Rochester called Restoration House.

00:11:10.266 --> 00:11:19.550
Dickens describes this house when he tells us about Satis House, where Miss Havisham lives.

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:26.422
Near Rochester, on the marshes, there is the village of Kooling.

00:11:26.482 --> 00:11:31.330
It has a churchyard with a lot of graves.

00:11:31.390 --> 00:11:39.034
At the beginning of the story, Pip meets the prisoner in this churchyard.

00:11:39.094 --> 00:11:46.960
The churchyard is near Gadshill Place, but Dickens is not here.

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:54.637
His body is in Westminster Abbey in London, in Poets Corner.

00:11:54.697 --> 00:12:01.486
This is a special part of the Abbey for famous writers.

00:12:01.546 --> 00:12:06.712
There is another village called chalk.

00:12:06.772 --> 00:12:10.414
Here you can see a forge.

00:12:10.474 --> 00:12:15.236
Dickens was in chalk for his honeymoon.

00:12:15.296 --> 00:12:19.958
Perhaps this is Joe's forge.

00:12:20.018 --> 00:12:25.991
Blacksmiths are very important in Victorian times.

00:12:26.051 --> 00:12:30.713
Horses are the main method of transport.

00:12:30.773 --> 00:12:34.486
Everyone needs horseshoes.

00:12:34.546 --> 00:12:39.989
People also need metal for other things.

00:12:40.049 --> 00:12:45.304
Do you know what is the most common English surname?

00:12:45.364 --> 00:12:47.555
It's Smith.

00:12:47.615 --> 00:12:51.398
Someone who works with metal.

00:12:51.458 --> 00:12:58.322
Joe Godgeri is poor, but he is very important.

00:12:58.382 --> 00:13:07.074
If you visit Rochester, you can also see Uncle Pumblechook's shop in the High Street.

00:13:07.134 --> 00:13:12.486
You can see the inn where there were the coaches for London.

00:13:12.546 --> 00:13:17.167
The mouth of the Thames is near Rochester.

00:13:17.227 --> 00:13:25.820
There is a great area of marshes, but the prison ships are not here now.

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:33.650
There are no blacksmiths, People don't travel to London by coach and horses.

00:13:33.710 --> 00:13:42.102
Everything is very different in the 21st century.

00:13:42.162 --> 00:13:52.866
Part 3 The Money Pip works with Joe.

00:13:52.926 --> 00:13:56.707
He loves Joe and Joe loves him.

00:13:56.767 --> 00:13:59.060
But Pip is unhappy.

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:01.794
because he isn't a gentleman.

00:14:01.854 --> 00:14:05.568
He is 18 years old now.

00:14:05.627 --> 00:14:11.912
When Pip's sister is ill, a young woman comes to help Joe.

00:14:11.972 --> 00:14:14.904
Her name is Biddy.

00:14:14.964 --> 00:14:20.238
She is kind, generous and very pretty.

00:14:20.298 --> 00:14:23.130
She likes Pip very much.

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:26.656
But Pip cannot forget Estella.

00:14:26.716 --> 00:14:28.852
I want to be a gentleman, Biddy.

00:14:28.912 --> 00:14:31.084
I want to marry Estella.

00:14:31.144 --> 00:14:33.826
I want to live in London.

00:14:33.886 --> 00:14:37.918
I am happy here with you and Joe, Pip.

00:14:37.978 --> 00:14:42.770
Joe isn't a gentleman, but he's a very good man.

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:44.812
Yes, you're right.

00:14:44.872 --> 00:14:48.474
But the marsh is a beautiful.

00:14:48.534 --> 00:14:52.046
I'm not a lady, and I'm not rich.

00:14:52.106 --> 00:14:55.584
But I like my life.

00:14:55.644 --> 00:15:00.674
One day, a visitor comes to the forge.

00:15:00.734 --> 00:15:03.598
His name is Mr. Jaggers.

00:15:03.658 --> 00:15:07.250
He is a lawyer from London.

00:15:07.310 --> 00:15:10.363
Is your name Pip?

00:15:10.422 --> 00:15:11.694
Yes, sir.

00:15:11.754 --> 00:15:14.306
I have news for you.

00:15:14.366 --> 00:15:16.117
You are rich.

00:15:16.177 --> 00:15:19.710
You have great expectations.

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:20.680
What?

00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:22.682
I don't understand.

00:15:22.743 --> 00:15:26.494
Someone wants to give you a lot of money.

00:15:26.555 --> 00:15:28.885
You must go to London.

00:15:28.945 --> 00:15:32.936
You must learn to be a gentleman.

00:15:32.996 --> 00:15:37.318
It is a big surprise for Pip.

00:15:37.378 --> 00:15:40.780
Joe and Biddy are very sad.

00:15:40.840 --> 00:15:43.432
They don't want to lose Pip.

00:15:43.492 --> 00:15:46.152
Who is my benefactor, sir?

00:15:46.212 --> 00:15:48.334
It's a secret.

00:15:48.394 --> 00:15:51.125
I must not tell you the name.

00:15:51.185 --> 00:15:53.496
Is it a man or a woman?

00:15:53.556 --> 00:15:55.658
I must not tell you.

00:15:55.719 --> 00:15:58.462
Don't ask any more questions.

00:15:58.522 --> 00:16:00.553
Take this money.

00:16:00.613 --> 00:16:03.835
Buy some gentlemen's clothes.

00:16:03.895 --> 00:16:06.767
Miss Havisham must be the person.

00:16:06.827 --> 00:16:09.148
She wants me to be a gentleman.

00:16:09.208 --> 00:16:11.920
She wants Estella to be a lady.

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:14.202
She wants us to marry.

00:16:14.262 --> 00:16:16.774
I am very happy.

00:16:16.834 --> 00:16:19.735
Pip leaves the village.

00:16:19.795 --> 00:16:22.697
Joe and Biddy are crying.

00:16:22.757 --> 00:16:24.962
But Pip is happy.

00:16:25.022 --> 00:16:27.268
He is in the coach.

00:16:27.328 --> 00:16:32.832
He is thinking about the future.

00:16:32.892 --> 00:16:37.146
Goodbye, Pip.

00:16:37.206 --> 00:16:38.736
Remember us?

00:16:38.796 --> 00:16:41.348
Good luck in London, Pip.

00:16:41.408 --> 00:16:44.771
Don't forget us when you're a fine gentleman.

00:16:44.831 --> 00:16:46.562
I'm going to London.

00:16:46.623 --> 00:16:48.224
I can't believe it.

00:16:48.284 --> 00:16:54.335
I want to see St Paul's Cathedral and Westminster Abbey and the Queen's Palace.

00:16:54.395 --> 00:16:55.982
I have money.

00:16:56.042 --> 00:16:58.214
I have new clothes.

00:16:58.274 --> 00:17:02.366
I am a gentleman.

00:17:02.426 --> 00:17:06.339
Part 4.

00:17:06.398 --> 00:17:11.992
London Pip arrives in London.

00:17:12.052 --> 00:17:16.104
He sees a big city for the first time.

00:17:16.164 --> 00:17:19.306
He forgets Joe and Biddy.

00:17:19.367 --> 00:17:22.973
He only thinks about Estella.

00:17:23.033 --> 00:17:27.300
He lives in Barnards Inn in London.

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:31.874
In his rooms, he meets Herbert Pocket.

00:17:31.934 --> 00:17:33.275
Hello.

00:17:33.335 --> 00:17:34.776
My name's Herbert.

00:17:34.836 --> 00:17:36.047
Hello.

00:17:36.107 --> 00:17:37.328
I'm Pip.

00:17:37.388 --> 00:17:38.899
I remember you.

00:17:38.959 --> 00:17:41.571
You're the boy in Miss Havisham's garden.

00:17:41.631 --> 00:17:42.642
Yes.

00:17:42.702 --> 00:17:44.663
But now we are friends.

00:17:44.723 --> 00:17:46.684
I want to show you London.

00:17:46.744 --> 00:17:48.566
My father is a teacher.

00:17:48.626 --> 00:17:50.778
He can help you to be a gentleman.

00:17:50.838 --> 00:17:53.886
Then I can marry a Stella.

00:17:53.946 --> 00:17:58.446
Herbert is telling Pip about Miss Havisham.

00:17:58.506 --> 00:18:01.848
He says, Be careful, Pip.

00:18:01.908 --> 00:18:04.400
Miss Havisham hates men.

00:18:04.460 --> 00:18:11.414
Many years ago, she was in love, but on her wedding day, the man wasn't at the church.

00:18:11.474 --> 00:18:14.376
The time was twenty to nine.

00:18:14.436 --> 00:18:17.858
Estella hates men too.

00:18:17.918 --> 00:18:20.780
I cannot marry you.

00:18:20.840 --> 00:18:25.490
I love your money, but I don't love you.

00:18:25.550 --> 00:18:29.538
Sir, this is terrible.

00:18:29.598 --> 00:18:31.508
Stop the clocks.

00:18:31.568 --> 00:18:33.998
Close the curtains.

00:18:34.058 --> 00:18:37.799
I don't want to live in the world."

00:18:37.859 --> 00:18:41.250
Pip learns to be a gentleman.

00:18:41.310 --> 00:18:43.971
He learns to eat politely.

00:18:44.031 --> 00:18:46.911
He learns to speak politely.

00:18:46.971 --> 00:18:50.362
He learns to behave politely.

00:18:50.422 --> 00:18:55.717
Joe visits him in London, but he doesn't stay long.

00:18:55.777 --> 00:19:00.854
Pip doesn't want to talk to his old friend, the blacksmith.

00:19:00.914 --> 00:19:03.786
Pip is a snob.

00:19:03.846 --> 00:19:07.100
You're a fine gentleman now, Pip.

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:09.592
You have fine clothes.

00:19:09.652 --> 00:19:11.132
Thank you, Joe.

00:19:11.192 --> 00:19:14.266
Biddy sends you her best wishes, Pip.

00:19:14.326 --> 00:19:16.006
Thank you, Joe.

00:19:16.067 --> 00:19:18.969
I'm going back to the village now, Pip.

00:19:19.029 --> 00:19:21.291
I don't belong in London.

00:19:21.351 --> 00:19:24.070
Goodbye, Joe.

00:19:24.130 --> 00:19:27.458
Joe is unhappy.

00:19:27.519 --> 00:19:29.840
He loves Pip.

00:19:29.900 --> 00:19:34.142
Pip buys new clothes and new furniture.

00:19:34.202 --> 00:19:38.846
Mr. Jagger's always has money to give him.

00:19:38.906 --> 00:19:44.318
Mr. Wemmick, my clerk, has some money for you, Pip.

00:19:44.378 --> 00:19:46.420
How much do you want?

00:19:46.480 --> 00:19:48.742
A lot, Mr. Jagger's.

00:19:48.802 --> 00:19:50.382
All right, Pip.

00:19:50.442 --> 00:19:53.310
You are 21 years old this year.

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:57.789
Your benefactor wants to give you more money.

00:19:57.850 --> 00:20:00.552
But who is my benefactor?

00:20:00.612 --> 00:20:02.593
It's Miss Havisham, isn't it?

00:20:02.653 --> 00:20:04.654
I cannot tell you.

00:20:04.714 --> 00:20:07.156
Here is your money, sir.

00:20:07.216 --> 00:20:10.410
Pip is very happy.

00:20:10.470 --> 00:20:13.221
He is a rich gentleman.

00:20:13.282 --> 00:20:17.764
He can marry Estella.

00:20:17.824 --> 00:20:21.877
Orphans.

00:20:21.937 --> 00:20:27.060
An orphan is a child without parents.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:36.638
There are two important orphans in the story of great expectations, Pip and Estella.

00:20:36.698 --> 00:20:41.741
Pip lives with his sister and Joe Godgeri.

00:20:41.802 --> 00:20:46.005
Estella lives with Miss Havisham.

00:20:46.065 --> 00:20:49.627
Who has the better life?

00:20:49.687 --> 00:21:01.683
Pip with his life on the marshes and Joe who loves him or is stellar with Miss Havisham's jewels and money.

00:21:01.744 --> 00:21:07.817
In the story, Pip looks for substitute fathers.

00:21:07.878 --> 00:21:13.360
As you read the story, think about this idea.

00:21:13.420 --> 00:21:18.067
Who takes the place of Pip's dead father?

00:21:18.127 --> 00:21:23.483
Who takes the place of Pip's dead mother?

00:21:23.544 --> 00:21:29.696
It is very hard to be an orphan in the 19th century.

00:21:29.756 --> 00:21:36.328
If you are rich, maybe there are rich relations who look after you.

00:21:36.388 --> 00:21:41.670
But if you are poor, no one helps you.

00:21:41.731 --> 00:21:47.091
There are a lot of orphans in the stories of Dickens.

00:21:47.151 --> 00:21:51.420
Oliver Twist is the most famous one.

00:21:51.481 --> 00:21:54.892
He must live in the workhouse.

00:21:54.952 --> 00:22:01.554
That is a place for poor people who have no money and no job.

00:22:01.614 --> 00:22:11.648
The local government gives them a place to live and food, but they must work and follow the rules.

00:22:11.708 --> 00:22:17.476
The food is bad and the work is hard.

00:22:17.536 --> 00:22:24.928
People in the times of Dickens are afraid of the workhouse.

00:22:24.988 --> 00:22:33.184
Some orphans live in special places called orphanages.

00:22:33.244 --> 00:22:38.519
Some of these orphanages are very bad.

00:22:38.579 --> 00:22:45.376
Dickens writes about another orphan in his book, David Copperfield.

00:22:45.436 --> 00:22:54.641
and another writer, Charlotte Bronte, writes about Jane Eyre, a girl orphan.

00:22:54.701 --> 00:23:00.623
Why are there a lot of orphans in Victorian times?

00:23:00.683 --> 00:23:07.265
Sometimes life is dangerous, especially for poor people.

00:23:07.325 --> 00:23:13.558
It is easy to die in an accident, in a factory or on a farm.

00:23:13.618 --> 00:23:18.724
Doctors and hospitals are not very advanced.

00:23:18.784 --> 00:23:23.136
Parents often die young from diseases.

00:23:23.196 --> 00:23:26.910
It is dangerous for women to have children.

00:23:26.970 --> 00:23:31.082
Women often die in childbirth.

00:23:31.142 --> 00:23:33.394
We are lucky.

00:23:33.454 --> 00:23:39.468
We live in the 21st century and health care is much better.

00:23:39.528 --> 00:23:44.524
We understand diseases better and how to avoid them.

00:23:44.584 --> 00:23:51.440
People do not live as long in Victorian times.

00:23:51.500 --> 00:24:03.208
Part 5 Estella in London Estella comes back from Paris.

00:24:03.268 --> 00:24:08.751
Now she is a lady and Pip is a gentleman.

00:24:08.811 --> 00:24:15.818
Pip goes to visit Miss Havisham at Satis House and meets Estella.

00:24:15.878 --> 00:24:21.204
Pip thinks that Miss Havisham is his benefactor.

00:24:21.264 --> 00:24:29.319
You're rich now, Pip, but the name of your benefactor is secret, I think.

00:24:29.379 --> 00:24:33.491
Yes, Miss Havisham, but I'm very grateful.

00:24:33.551 --> 00:24:35.112
Good.

00:24:35.172 --> 00:24:38.714
Look, here is Estella.

00:24:38.774 --> 00:24:43.584
You are very beautiful, Estella.

00:24:43.644 --> 00:24:46.692
It's the blacksmith's boy.

00:24:46.752 --> 00:24:48.823
You are a gentleman now.

00:24:48.883 --> 00:24:52.065
Your shoes are clean.

00:24:52.125 --> 00:24:55.807
Miss Havisham is happy.

00:24:55.867 --> 00:25:00.370
She wants Estella to break the hearts of men.

00:25:00.430 --> 00:25:04.342
This is Miss Havisham's revenge.

00:25:04.402 --> 00:25:06.603
Is she beautiful?

00:25:06.663 --> 00:25:08.234
She asks Pip.

00:25:08.294 --> 00:25:10.955
Yes, he says.

00:25:11.015 --> 00:25:13.126
Love her Pip.

00:25:13.186 --> 00:25:14.938
Says Miss Havisham.

00:25:14.998 --> 00:25:20.413
Love her, love her, love her.

00:25:20.473 --> 00:25:24.126
Estella comes to London.

00:25:24.186 --> 00:25:29.750
Pip is her friend, but she flirts with a lot of men.

00:25:29.810 --> 00:25:32.422
Pip is jealous.

00:25:32.482 --> 00:25:36.986
At a party, he is talking to Estella.

00:25:37.047 --> 00:25:40.879
Estella, don't dance with other men.

00:25:40.939 --> 00:25:42.800
Don't smile at them.

00:25:42.860 --> 00:25:43.901
Marry me.

00:25:43.921 --> 00:25:46.273
I am a gentleman now.

00:25:46.333 --> 00:25:48.074
I love you.

00:25:48.134 --> 00:25:50.466
Don't be silly, Pip.

00:25:50.526 --> 00:25:52.178
I have no heart.

00:25:52.238 --> 00:25:54.139
I cannot love you.

00:25:54.199 --> 00:25:56.620
I can only make you unhappy.

00:25:56.680 --> 00:26:00.334
Do you want to dance, Miss Estella?

00:26:00.394 --> 00:26:02.525
Yes, thank you, sir.

00:26:02.585 --> 00:26:06.774
Goodbye, Pip.

00:26:06.834 --> 00:26:12.384
Pip is very sad.

00:26:12.444 --> 00:26:15.726
Herbert wants to help his friend.

00:26:15.786 --> 00:26:19.029
He tells him to forget Estella.

00:26:19.090 --> 00:26:22.792
But I love her, says Pip.

00:26:22.852 --> 00:26:28.106
Pip is drinking with Herbert and some other students.

00:26:28.166 --> 00:26:31.800
Every man drinks to a lady.

00:26:31.860 --> 00:26:34.792
Bentley Drummel is there.

00:26:34.852 --> 00:26:40.816
He is rich and handsome, but he has a bad reputation.

00:26:40.876 --> 00:26:43.457
He raises his glass.

00:26:43.517 --> 00:26:49.530
To Estella, the most beautiful woman in London.

00:26:49.590 --> 00:26:52.182
Bip is angry.

00:26:52.242 --> 00:26:54.933
You cannot drink to Estella.

00:26:54.993 --> 00:26:56.864
You don't know her.

00:26:56.924 --> 00:26:58.273
Why not?

00:26:58.333 --> 00:27:00.672
I know her well.

00:27:00.732 --> 00:27:03.234
She is my special friend.

00:27:03.294 --> 00:27:05.956
I often dance with her.

00:27:06.016 --> 00:27:08.358
You are lying!

00:27:08.418 --> 00:27:11.810
Herbert tells Pip to be careful.

00:27:11.870 --> 00:27:14.662
Everyone is listening.

00:27:14.722 --> 00:27:20.897
Later, Bentley Drummel shows everybody a letter from Estella.

00:27:20.957 --> 00:27:26.995
She writes, Yes, I know Mr. Drummel.

00:27:27.055 --> 00:27:29.497
Sometimes I dance with him.

00:27:29.557 --> 00:27:31.188
Estella.

00:27:31.249 --> 00:27:34.090
Pip must apologise.

00:27:34.150 --> 00:27:36.802
I am sorry, he says.

00:27:36.862 --> 00:27:38.164
You are right.

00:27:38.224 --> 00:27:40.475
You are not a liar.

00:27:40.535 --> 00:27:44.628
And you, sir, are not a gentleman.

00:27:44.688 --> 00:27:51.022
The other students laugh at Pip.

00:27:51.082 --> 00:27:56.915
Pip goes to see Estella.

00:27:56.975 --> 00:28:00.888
Estella, why do you see Bentley Drummel?

00:28:00.948 --> 00:28:03.230
Estella answers.

00:28:03.290 --> 00:28:06.892
There are lots of men in my life, Pip.

00:28:06.952 --> 00:28:09.434
I am very beautiful.

00:28:09.494 --> 00:28:13.077
Miss Havisham gives me a lot of money.

00:28:13.138 --> 00:28:15.769
They all want to marry me.

00:28:15.830 --> 00:28:20.273
But Estella, Drummel is a horrible person.

00:28:20.333 --> 00:28:23.442
His cruel and stupid.

00:28:23.502 --> 00:28:28.612
I like cruel, stupid, rich men.

00:28:28.672 --> 00:28:30.273
Remember, Pip?

00:28:30.333 --> 00:28:32.374
I have no heart.

00:28:32.434 --> 00:28:35.408
Biddy writes to Pip.

00:28:35.468 --> 00:28:40.471
Pip's sister, Joe's wife, is dead.

00:28:40.532 --> 00:28:43.574
Pip goes back to the village.

00:28:43.634 --> 00:28:48.067
After the funeral, he speaks to Biddy.

00:28:48.127 --> 00:28:51.682
Joe is very sad, Pip.

00:28:51.742 --> 00:28:55.296
You never write to him, or visit us.

00:28:55.356 --> 00:28:56.867
I'm sorry, Biddy.

00:28:56.927 --> 00:28:58.268
But don't worry.

00:28:58.328 --> 00:29:01.161
I want to visit Joe often now.

00:29:01.221 --> 00:29:04.774
My sister is dead, and he is alone.

00:29:04.834 --> 00:29:07.216
I don't believe you, Pip.

00:29:07.276 --> 00:29:12.401
You're a gentleman now, and you don't want to remember Joe and me.

00:29:12.461 --> 00:29:13.592
No, Biddy.

00:29:13.652 --> 00:29:15.614
I miss you.

00:29:15.674 --> 00:29:19.398
But Pip doesn't visit them.

00:29:19.458 --> 00:29:24.424
He always thinks about Estella and Miss Havisham.

00:29:24.484 --> 00:29:30.250
He forgets his real friends.

00:29:30.310 --> 00:29:35.004
Part 6.

00:29:35.064 --> 00:29:41.912
The Visitor One night, Pip is studying at home.

00:29:41.972 --> 00:29:44.988
It is a dark stormy night.

00:29:45.048 --> 00:29:49.615
He can hear the wind and the rain in the London streets.

00:29:49.675 --> 00:29:54.938
Suddenly, somebody knocks at the door.

00:29:54.998 --> 00:30:00.570
It is an old, rough looking man.

00:30:00.630 --> 00:30:03.432
He is not a gentleman.

00:30:03.492 --> 00:30:04.872
Who are you?

00:30:04.933 --> 00:30:06.443
What do you want?

00:30:06.504 --> 00:30:07.864
My boy.

00:30:07.884 --> 00:30:09.825
My boy.

00:30:09.885 --> 00:30:12.345
Do you recognize me?

00:30:12.405 --> 00:30:15.186
No, I don't know you.

00:30:15.246 --> 00:30:17.216
Please go away.

00:30:17.276 --> 00:30:19.246
But I know you.

00:30:19.307 --> 00:30:22.387
You are my gentleman.

00:30:22.447 --> 00:30:24.358
This is a mistake.

00:30:24.418 --> 00:30:27.428
No, there's no mistake.

00:30:27.488 --> 00:30:31.489
You are a gentleman because you have my money.

00:30:31.549 --> 00:30:34.519
You are my gentleman.

00:30:34.580 --> 00:30:38.734
Pip and the prisoner are talking.

00:30:38.794 --> 00:30:41.350
Do you remember the marshes?

00:30:41.410 --> 00:30:44.222
Do you remember the churchyard?

00:30:44.282 --> 00:30:47.024
Do you remember the prisoner?

00:30:47.084 --> 00:30:49.516
I am the prisoner.

00:30:49.576 --> 00:30:53.368
My name is Abel Magwitch.

00:30:53.428 --> 00:30:55.880
But this is impossible.

00:30:55.941 --> 00:30:57.742
No, dear boy.

00:30:57.802 --> 00:30:59.553
You helped me.

00:30:59.613 --> 00:31:01.924
I remember the food.

00:31:01.984 --> 00:31:04.676
I was a prisoner in Australia.

00:31:04.736 --> 00:31:07.716
Now I have a lot of money.

00:31:07.776 --> 00:31:10.824
I have a sheep farm in Australia.

00:31:10.884 --> 00:31:14.055
Jagger's is my lawyer.

00:31:14.115 --> 00:31:18.437
He gives you money from me, dear boy.

00:31:18.497 --> 00:31:21.548
I am in England to see you.

00:31:21.608 --> 00:31:25.060
Pip is very upset.

00:31:25.120 --> 00:31:26.891
I don't understand.

00:31:26.951 --> 00:31:29.702
Miss Havisham is my benefactor.

00:31:29.762 --> 00:31:31.423
Magwitch answers.

00:31:31.484 --> 00:31:32.724
No, no.

00:31:32.784 --> 00:31:34.345
You are wrong.

00:31:34.405 --> 00:31:36.407
This is terrible.

00:31:36.467 --> 00:31:38.418
I cannot take your money.

00:31:38.478 --> 00:31:40.739
I cannot marry Estella.

00:31:40.799 --> 00:31:43.320
I hate you."

00:31:43.380 --> 00:31:47.410
Now Pip knows the truth.

00:31:47.470 --> 00:31:50.951
He tells everything to his friends.

00:31:51.011 --> 00:31:53.892
It is dangerous for Abel Pip.

00:31:53.952 --> 00:31:56.002
The police want to hang him.

00:31:56.062 --> 00:31:57.912
We must help him.

00:31:57.972 --> 00:32:01.548
Magwitch must return to Australia.

00:32:01.608 --> 00:32:04.223
It is the end of my dreams.

00:32:04.284 --> 00:32:06.506
I am poor again.

00:32:06.566 --> 00:32:09.878
Abel Magwitch must hide from the police.

00:32:09.938 --> 00:32:12.990
His enemy is looking for him.

00:32:13.050 --> 00:32:16.194
I am happy with you, Pip.

00:32:16.254 --> 00:32:18.716
You are like my son.

00:32:18.776 --> 00:32:20.376
I love you.

00:32:20.436 --> 00:32:24.050
I don't want to go back to Australia.

00:32:24.110 --> 00:32:28.012
Pip decides to help Magwitch.

00:32:28.072 --> 00:32:31.126
They must go to Australia together.

00:32:31.186 --> 00:32:35.877
First, he wants to see Joe and Biddy again.

00:32:35.937 --> 00:32:40.578
He goes back to the forge in the country.

00:32:40.638 --> 00:32:45.000
Pip, I'm so glad to see you.

00:32:45.060 --> 00:32:46.630
How are you?

00:32:46.690 --> 00:32:51.722
I'm sorry we have no good food or fine wine for a gentleman like you.

00:32:51.782 --> 00:32:53.492
Don't say that, Joe.

00:32:53.552 --> 00:32:55.782
I'm not a gentleman now.

00:32:55.842 --> 00:32:59.673
It's a long story and I cannot tell you everything.

00:32:59.734 --> 00:33:01.614
It's a secret.

00:33:01.674 --> 00:33:04.094
But I'm here to say goodbye.

00:33:04.154 --> 00:33:05.596
Goodbye.

00:33:05.656 --> 00:33:07.548
Where are you going?

00:33:07.608 --> 00:33:09.760
I'm going to Australia.

00:33:09.820 --> 00:33:11.592
I cannot tell you anymore.

00:33:11.652 --> 00:33:14.614
But thank you, Joe, and Biddy for everything.

00:33:14.674 --> 00:33:19.628
You are my best friends.

00:33:19.688 --> 00:33:25.994
Ladies and gentlemen.

00:33:26.054 --> 00:33:29.608
The 18th century.

00:33:29.668 --> 00:33:36.042
In the 18th century, everyone has a place in society.

00:33:36.102 --> 00:33:39.764
It is almost impossible to change.

00:33:39.824 --> 00:33:46.836
If a man belongs to a rich, important family, he is a gentleman.

00:33:46.896 --> 00:33:58.640
If a man belongs to a poor, unimportant family, he is an ordinary person, and he can never be a gentleman.

00:33:58.700 --> 00:34:02.798
It is the same for women.

00:34:02.858 --> 00:34:07.406
the 19th century.

00:34:07.467 --> 00:34:12.768
In the time of Queen Victoria, it is different.

00:34:12.828 --> 00:34:20.910
Even a poor person can become a gentleman or a lady by working hard and becoming rich.

00:34:20.970 --> 00:34:25.192
It is not easy, but it is possible.

00:34:25.252 --> 00:34:32.302
It is the first time in history that people can change their place in society.

00:34:32.363 --> 00:34:36.764
Dickens himself is a good example.

00:34:36.824 --> 00:34:40.036
He comes from a poor family.

00:34:40.096 --> 00:34:43.867
His father is sometimes in prison.

00:34:43.928 --> 00:34:50.731
Dickens must work in a factory when he is a child to help his family.

00:34:50.791 --> 00:34:56.144
But Dickens begins to write and becomes popular.

00:34:56.204 --> 00:34:59.126
He makes a lot of money.

00:34:59.187 --> 00:35:02.736
He is intelligent and educated.

00:35:02.797 --> 00:35:06.198
He is a gentleman.

00:35:06.258 --> 00:35:12.924
In the story, Pip is also poor, but becomes a gentleman.

00:35:12.984 --> 00:35:17.538
First, he uses his benefactors money.

00:35:17.598 --> 00:35:27.246
But, at the end of the story, he works hard for eleven years in the East and has his own money.

00:35:27.306 --> 00:35:31.426
What is a gentleman?

00:35:31.486 --> 00:35:36.133
In the story, Drummel is a gentleman.

00:35:36.193 --> 00:35:45.045
He belongs to a rich, important family, but he is cruel and stupid.

00:35:45.105 --> 00:35:49.956
When Pip is a boy, he is not a gentleman.

00:35:50.016 --> 00:35:56.148
Estella says that he has dirty boots and rough hands.

00:35:56.208 --> 00:36:02.380
Pip is a gentleman after he learns how to behave well.

00:36:02.440 --> 00:36:06.662
But where does his money come from?

00:36:06.722 --> 00:36:10.574
Joe is not a gentleman.

00:36:10.634 --> 00:36:14.286
He is poor and must work hard.

00:36:14.346 --> 00:36:17.138
He cannot read and write.

00:36:17.198 --> 00:36:21.100
But he is very kind and good.

00:36:21.160 --> 00:36:24.811
Who is the real gentleman?

00:36:24.871 --> 00:36:28.472
What do you think?

00:36:28.532 --> 00:36:32.687
What is a lady?

00:36:32.747 --> 00:36:38.534
Miss Havisham belongs to a rich, important family.

00:36:38.594 --> 00:36:48.480
Her money comes from her father, but she lives in a big house without daylight or time.

00:36:48.540 --> 00:36:53.164
Estella learns to be a lady in Paris.

00:36:53.224 --> 00:36:59.818
She has money and jewels, but she has no heart.

00:36:59.878 --> 00:37:02.728
Biddy is poor.

00:37:02.788 --> 00:37:05.007
and must work hard.

00:37:05.067 --> 00:37:10.028
But she is kind and helps other people.

00:37:10.088 --> 00:37:14.439
Who is the real lady?

00:37:14.499 --> 00:37:19.980
Marriage is very important for Victorian ladies.

00:37:20.040 --> 00:37:28.942
If a man promises to marry a woman and then breaks his promise, the law punishes him.

00:37:29.002 --> 00:37:32.092
Be careful boys.

00:37:32.152 --> 00:37:39.518
It is a terrible thing for Ms Havisham when her fiancé doesn't marry her.

00:37:39.578 --> 00:37:45.572
She almost goes crazy.

00:37:45.632 --> 00:37:50.616
Part seven.

00:37:50.676 --> 00:37:53.078
Fire.

00:37:53.138 --> 00:37:57.221
Pip wants to see Ms Havisham again.

00:37:57.282 --> 00:38:00.223
He visits Satis House.

00:38:00.284 --> 00:38:04.556
Estella is with Ms Havisham.

00:38:04.616 --> 00:38:07.676
Why are you here?

00:38:07.736 --> 00:38:09.378
I know everything.

00:38:09.438 --> 00:38:11.548
You're not my benefactor.

00:38:11.608 --> 00:38:13.690
You don't care about me.

00:38:13.750 --> 00:38:15.940
I'm sorry, Pip.

00:38:16.000 --> 00:38:18.782
Estella, marry me.

00:38:18.842 --> 00:38:21.784
I'm poor again, but I love you.

00:38:21.844 --> 00:38:23.364
No, Pip.

00:38:23.424 --> 00:38:25.205
I cannot marry you.

00:38:25.265 --> 00:38:28.476
I want to marry Bentley Drummel.

00:38:28.536 --> 00:38:32.828
Pip and Miss Havisham are shocked.

00:38:32.888 --> 00:38:36.650
I know nothing about this.

00:38:36.710 --> 00:38:38.752
I cannot believe it.

00:38:38.812 --> 00:38:40.994
It is true, Miss Havisham.

00:38:41.054 --> 00:38:44.077
I want to be Mrs. Bentley Drummel.

00:38:44.137 --> 00:38:46.348
Forget me, Pip.

00:38:46.408 --> 00:38:53.496
Ungrateful girl, you have my money and my jewels and my love.

00:38:53.556 --> 00:38:56.538
I don't want you to marry a man.

00:38:56.598 --> 00:38:58.920
I hate all men.

00:38:58.980 --> 00:39:01.846
I want you here with me.

00:39:01.906 --> 00:39:05.062
Do you love me, Estella?

00:39:05.122 --> 00:39:07.253
No, Miss Havisham.

00:39:07.313 --> 00:39:09.014
I cannot love.

00:39:09.074 --> 00:39:10.966
I have no heart.

00:39:11.026 --> 00:39:13.646
That is your lesson to me.

00:39:13.706 --> 00:39:16.098
Goodbye, Pip.

00:39:16.158 --> 00:39:19.130
This is your fault, Miss Havisham.

00:39:19.190 --> 00:39:22.112
You are a bitter old woman.

00:39:22.172 --> 00:39:26.878
Estella has no heart because you taught her to hate men.

00:39:26.938 --> 00:39:29.291
She doesn't love Drummel.

00:39:29.351 --> 00:39:33.123
He is rich and handsome, but he is cruel.

00:39:33.183 --> 00:39:35.444
It is a terrible marriage.

00:39:35.504 --> 00:39:37.766
You are responsible.

00:39:37.826 --> 00:39:40.006
Goodbye.

00:39:40.066 --> 00:39:44.038
Pip leaves Satis House.

00:39:44.098 --> 00:39:47.150
Pip returns to London.

00:39:47.210 --> 00:39:51.753
There, someone gives Pip a letter from Wemmick.

00:39:51.813 --> 00:39:55.847
It says, don't go home.

00:39:55.907 --> 00:39:59.170
Pip visits Wemmick.

00:39:59.230 --> 00:40:02.060
Madgwich has a lot of enemies.

00:40:02.120 --> 00:40:04.231
They know he is in London.

00:40:04.291 --> 00:40:08.072
They are following you because they want to find him.

00:40:08.132 --> 00:40:10.913
Abel must hide from them.

00:40:10.973 --> 00:40:15.224
Abel must stay with my friend, Clara, and her father.

00:40:15.284 --> 00:40:17.265
They live near the river.

00:40:17.325 --> 00:40:23.637
Pip agrees, but Miss Havisham asks him to visit her again.

00:40:23.697 --> 00:40:26.889
He goes back to Satis house.

00:40:26.949 --> 00:40:28.770
She says...

00:40:28.830 --> 00:40:30.982
You are sad.

00:40:31.042 --> 00:40:34.724
A Stella is married to a terrible man.

00:40:34.784 --> 00:40:37.155
It is my fault.

00:40:37.215 --> 00:40:39.346
Do you forgive me?

00:40:39.406 --> 00:40:40.737
Yes.

00:40:40.797 --> 00:40:42.168
I forgive you.

00:40:42.228 --> 00:40:43.718
Says Pip.

00:40:43.738 --> 00:40:46.160
I want to help you Pip.

00:40:46.180 --> 00:40:48.050
I want to give you money.

00:40:48.110 --> 00:40:50.792
I have a human heart.

00:40:50.852 --> 00:40:52.293
Thank you.

00:40:52.353 --> 00:40:54.614
But nobody can help me.

00:40:54.674 --> 00:40:56.978
I want a Stella.

00:40:57.038 --> 00:41:01.082
Miss Havisham is sitting near the fire.

00:41:01.142 --> 00:41:05.933
Suddenly, her old wedding dress touches the fire.

00:41:05.993 --> 00:41:08.554
It begins to burn.

00:41:08.614 --> 00:41:14.146
Pip saves her, but the old clothes burn quickly.

00:41:14.206 --> 00:41:17.268
She is badly injured.

00:41:17.328 --> 00:41:19.879
Poor Miss Havisham.

00:41:19.939 --> 00:41:22.810
She has nothing now.

00:41:22.870 --> 00:41:26.005
He waits for the doctor.

00:41:26.065 --> 00:41:28.280
Then he thinks.

00:41:28.341 --> 00:41:31.444
I would like to see Joe and Biddy.

00:41:31.504 --> 00:41:33.826
They really love me.

00:41:33.886 --> 00:41:35.998
But I have no time.

00:41:36.058 --> 00:41:38.270
I must go back to London.

00:41:38.330 --> 00:41:40.972
I must save Abel Magwitch.

00:41:41.033 --> 00:41:46.458
His enemies want to catch him.

00:41:46.518 --> 00:41:51.032
Part eight.

00:41:51.092 --> 00:41:53.492
The escape.

00:41:53.552 --> 00:41:57.651
Wemic is helping Pip and Herbert.

00:41:57.711 --> 00:42:01.022
Magwitch must go back to Australia.

00:42:01.082 --> 00:42:03.452
They make a plan.

00:42:03.512 --> 00:42:06.243
There is a ship to Hamburg.

00:42:06.303 --> 00:42:10.014
You can meet it at the end of the River Thames.

00:42:10.074 --> 00:42:14.284
But no one must see you when you leave London.

00:42:14.344 --> 00:42:16.492
What can we do?

00:42:16.552 --> 00:42:19.340
Row on the river every day.

00:42:19.400 --> 00:42:22.140
Do the same thing every day.

00:42:22.200 --> 00:42:25.912
But one day, take Magwich with you.

00:42:25.972 --> 00:42:30.742
Row to the end of the Thames where it meets the sea.

00:42:30.803 --> 00:42:33.623
Catch the ship to Hamburg.

00:42:33.684 --> 00:42:36.654
Then go to Australia.

00:42:36.714 --> 00:42:39.675
Then Magwich is safe.

00:42:39.735 --> 00:42:41.966
That's a great idea.

00:42:42.026 --> 00:42:44.009
Let's do it.

00:42:44.069 --> 00:42:49.844
One night, Pip and Herbert take their boat to meet Magwich.

00:42:49.904 --> 00:42:52.746
He is wearing a disguise.

00:42:52.806 --> 00:43:00.250
They row towards the sea at the end of the Great River Thames.

00:43:00.310 --> 00:43:05.183
Thank you, Pip, my boy.

00:43:05.243 --> 00:43:08.655
But I don't want to be alone in Australia.

00:43:08.715 --> 00:43:10.546
Don't worry, Abel.

00:43:10.606 --> 00:43:12.240
I'm coming with you.

00:43:12.300 --> 00:43:14.734
There is nothing in England for me.

00:43:14.794 --> 00:43:17.086
Estello is married.

00:43:17.146 --> 00:43:19.778
I am very happy, Pip.

00:43:19.838 --> 00:43:21.880
You are my son.

00:43:21.940 --> 00:43:25.243
I want you to be with me.

00:43:25.303 --> 00:43:27.484
Shh.

00:43:27.544 --> 00:43:29.896
I think that someone is following us.

00:43:29.956 --> 00:43:31.708
We must be careful.

00:43:31.768 --> 00:43:36.211
The police mustn't catch Maguich in England.

00:43:36.271 --> 00:43:41.264
They continue to go down the river.

00:43:41.324 --> 00:43:45.835
They hide on an island during the night.

00:43:45.896 --> 00:43:50.179
In the morning, they are looking for the big ship.

00:43:50.239 --> 00:43:56.234
Pip and Magwitch are going to Europe and then to Australia.

00:43:56.294 --> 00:43:59.097
They are escaping.

00:43:59.157 --> 00:44:02.120
They see the ship.

00:44:02.180 --> 00:44:05.112
But there is another boat.

00:44:05.172 --> 00:44:09.774
There are three policemen in it and another man.

00:44:09.834 --> 00:44:11.432
Look.

00:44:11.492 --> 00:44:13.003
There's the ship.

00:44:13.063 --> 00:44:14.694
Row quickly.

00:44:14.754 --> 00:44:16.805
We must catch it.

00:44:16.865 --> 00:44:18.836
That's Magwitch.

00:44:18.896 --> 00:44:20.487
Abel Magwitch.

00:44:20.547 --> 00:44:21.667
Stop.

00:44:21.727 --> 00:44:24.579
That man is a prisoner from Australia.

00:44:24.639 --> 00:44:25.999
You mustn't help him.

00:44:26.059 --> 00:44:27.060
Stop.

00:44:27.120 --> 00:44:28.720
Row faster.

00:44:28.780 --> 00:44:29.991
Faster.

00:44:30.051 --> 00:44:32.302
We must catch the ship.

00:44:32.362 --> 00:44:36.058
Who is that man in the boat with the police?

00:44:36.118 --> 00:44:38.783
I think that I can recognize him.

00:44:38.843 --> 00:44:42.286
It's my enemy, Compison.

00:44:42.346 --> 00:44:47.758
Yes, the man in the other boat is Compison.

00:44:47.819 --> 00:44:51.431
He is the other prisoner from the marshes.

00:44:51.491 --> 00:44:55.954
He is helping the police because he hates maguage.

00:44:56.014 --> 00:44:59.266
And maguage hates him.

00:44:59.326 --> 00:45:03.948
Pip and Herbert row quickly towards the ship.

00:45:04.008 --> 00:45:06.993
But the police are catching them.

00:45:07.053 --> 00:45:09.958
Magwitch is very angry.

00:45:10.018 --> 00:45:12.450
He hates Compperson.

00:45:12.511 --> 00:45:16.664
He jumps in the other boat and fights Compperson.

00:45:16.725 --> 00:45:20.358
They fall in the water.

00:45:20.418 --> 00:45:25.472
The big ship passes over them.

00:45:25.533 --> 00:45:27.524
Are they dead?

00:45:27.584 --> 00:45:33.326
Pip dives in the sea to rescue Magwitch.

00:45:33.386 --> 00:45:37.464
We arrest you, Abel Magwitch.

00:45:37.524 --> 00:45:39.995
But where is Compasson?

00:45:40.055 --> 00:45:41.486
He's dead.

00:45:41.546 --> 00:45:44.647
The wheels of the ship are very powerful.

00:45:44.707 --> 00:45:47.508
His body is in the water.

00:45:47.568 --> 00:45:49.089
Come with us.

00:45:49.149 --> 00:45:51.310
We are going back to London.

00:45:51.370 --> 00:45:53.411
We are going to prison.

00:45:53.471 --> 00:45:55.712
This man must die.

00:45:55.772 --> 00:45:56.292
No!

00:45:56.312 --> 00:45:59.043
He is like my father.

00:45:59.103 --> 00:46:04.280
Please don't take him.

00:46:04.340 --> 00:46:11.118
transportation to Australia.

00:46:11.178 --> 00:46:14.929
This is the 18th century.

00:46:14.989 --> 00:46:19.690
The punishment for many crimes is hanging.

00:46:19.750 --> 00:46:26.082
Thieves and robbers, not only murderers, must hang.

00:46:26.142 --> 00:46:30.443
But this is a problem for the government.

00:46:30.503 --> 00:46:33.594
There are too many criminals.

00:46:33.654 --> 00:46:37.931
We need a new way of punishing them.

00:46:37.992 --> 00:46:42.729
The answer is transportation.

00:46:42.789 --> 00:46:48.040
This means sending criminals to Australia.

00:46:48.100 --> 00:46:51.540
Why is this a good idea?

00:46:51.600 --> 00:46:56.641
Because the thieves and robbers leave England.

00:46:56.702 --> 00:47:01.352
They can help to build a new country.

00:47:01.413 --> 00:47:05.456
What are the prison ships?

00:47:05.516 --> 00:47:09.803
These are old ships on the Thames.

00:47:09.862 --> 00:47:13.266
The Navy does not need them.

00:47:13.326 --> 00:47:16.318
They are horrible places.

00:47:16.379 --> 00:47:20.932
They are wet and dark and smelly.

00:47:20.993 --> 00:47:25.516
The convicts stay here for several months.

00:47:25.576 --> 00:47:29.400
Then they go to Australia.

00:47:29.460 --> 00:47:33.632
Some of them are dangerous criminals.

00:47:33.692 --> 00:47:38.262
they must stay in Australia for life.

00:47:38.322 --> 00:47:42.694
Some of them commit small crimes.

00:47:42.754 --> 00:47:47.446
A servant girl steals something from a shop.

00:47:47.506 --> 00:47:52.668
She goes to Australia for seven years.

00:47:52.728 --> 00:47:58.380
How do the prisoners travel to Australia?

00:47:58.440 --> 00:48:02.651
It is 15,000 miles to Australia.

00:48:02.711 --> 00:48:07.494
The journey takes 100 days.

00:48:07.554 --> 00:48:11.136
Ships take the prisoners.

00:48:11.196 --> 00:48:15.558
Between 1787 and 1868, 162,000 male and female prisoners go from Britain to Australia.

00:48:15.578 --> 00:48:17.289
The ships are not good places.

00:48:17.349 --> 00:48:26.247
A lot of prisoners die from diseases.

00:48:26.307 --> 00:48:37.936
They have no fresh air below decks.

00:48:37.996 --> 00:48:45.221
The punishments for prisoners who make trouble are very hard.

00:48:45.281 --> 00:48:50.124
What happens in Australia?

00:48:50.184 --> 00:48:54.596
In Australia, the prisoners work.

00:48:54.656 --> 00:48:58.158
They help to build new towns.

00:48:58.218 --> 00:49:04.151
Sometimes they become free men and women after a few years.

00:49:04.211 --> 00:49:11.282
Often they become important, well known and respectable people.

00:49:11.342 --> 00:49:22.287
The first farmers, brewers, millers etc. in Australia are convicts.

00:49:22.347 --> 00:49:26.138
In 1805 Solomon Wiseman is a prisoner.

00:49:26.158 --> 00:49:31.038
In 1833 he is Governor of Sydney.

00:49:31.098 --> 00:49:38.212
But the serious criminals must not return to England.

00:49:38.272 --> 00:49:45.246
If they do, and the police catch them, the punishment is death.

00:49:45.306 --> 00:49:49.378
Do the Victorians hang murderers?

00:49:49.438 --> 00:49:51.100
Yes.

00:49:51.160 --> 00:49:54.782
Public hangings are very popular.

00:49:54.842 --> 00:49:59.726
In the story, Pip lives near Newgate prison.

00:49:59.786 --> 00:50:02.651
They hang people there.

00:50:02.711 --> 00:50:06.178
Large crowds watch.

00:50:06.238 --> 00:50:09.250
Some people pay ten pounds.

00:50:09.310 --> 00:50:14.384
A lot of money in Victorian England for a good seat.

00:50:14.444 --> 00:50:19.538
Dickens himself attends one hanging in London.

00:50:19.598 --> 00:50:21.640
He hates it.

00:50:21.700 --> 00:50:29.280
He says that he lives in a city of devils.

00:50:29.340 --> 00:50:33.886
Part 9.

00:50:33.946 --> 00:50:37.306
Joe to the rescue.

00:50:37.366 --> 00:50:42.689
The police take Pip and Magwitch back to London.

00:50:42.749 --> 00:50:45.260
I am very cold.

00:50:45.320 --> 00:50:48.121
The river is very cold.

00:50:48.181 --> 00:50:51.132
My head is bleeding.

00:50:51.192 --> 00:50:53.863
Let me hold you in my arms.

00:50:53.923 --> 00:50:56.294
Magwitch is our prisoner.

00:50:56.354 --> 00:50:59.709
He must wear chains.

00:50:59.769 --> 00:51:03.906
Now there is a big problem.

00:51:03.966 --> 00:51:05.916
The police say...

00:51:05.976 --> 00:51:08.339
We must hang Magwitch.

00:51:08.399 --> 00:51:10.200
He is a criminal.

00:51:10.261 --> 00:51:13.102
But Magwitch is very ill.

00:51:13.162 --> 00:51:15.515
He is dying.

00:51:15.575 --> 00:51:19.438
Pip is visiting him in prison.

00:51:19.498 --> 00:51:22.600
Abel, I have no father.

00:51:22.660 --> 00:51:24.822
So you are my father now.

00:51:24.882 --> 00:51:26.744
I love you.

00:51:26.804 --> 00:51:30.878
Dear boy, I love you.

00:51:30.938 --> 00:51:34.119
You're my fine gentleman.

00:51:34.179 --> 00:51:36.010
Are you happy?

00:51:36.070 --> 00:51:37.270
No.

00:51:37.330 --> 00:51:39.361
I cannot be happy.

00:51:39.421 --> 00:51:41.592
I love a beautiful woman.

00:51:41.652 --> 00:51:46.723
Her name is Estella, but she is the wife of another man.

00:51:46.784 --> 00:51:50.184
I hope you're happy soon, Pip.

00:51:50.245 --> 00:51:52.356
Goodbye.

00:51:52.416 --> 00:51:56.476
I don't have a long time to live.

00:51:56.536 --> 00:52:00.473
Abel Magwitch dies.

00:52:00.533 --> 00:52:03.840
Pip is very sad.

00:52:03.900 --> 00:52:06.031
He has no money.

00:52:06.091 --> 00:52:12.786
He has no friends in London because Herbert is working in another country.

00:52:12.846 --> 00:52:16.428
Pip owes money to the shopkeepers.

00:52:16.488 --> 00:52:22.000
They are very angry with him and take him to a house.

00:52:22.060 --> 00:52:27.664
If he wants to be free, he must pay the money.

00:52:27.724 --> 00:52:31.270
Pip is very ill.

00:52:31.330 --> 00:52:35.076
He's dreaming about his childhood.

00:52:35.136 --> 00:52:38.358
He's dreaming about Joe.

00:52:38.418 --> 00:52:40.778
His best friend.

00:52:40.838 --> 00:52:43.940
Then he wakes up.

00:52:44.000 --> 00:52:46.420
Joe is there.

00:52:46.480 --> 00:52:49.011
Come home with me, Pip.

00:52:49.071 --> 00:52:52.242
I have enough money to pay the shopkeepers.

00:52:52.303 --> 00:52:54.042
You are free.

00:52:54.102 --> 00:52:56.943
But you are poor Joe.

00:52:57.003 --> 00:52:59.054
Money is not important.

00:52:59.114 --> 00:53:04.146
You are important because Biddy and I love you.

00:53:04.206 --> 00:53:08.377
Pip goes back to the country.

00:53:08.437 --> 00:53:11.458
He lives at the forge again.

00:53:11.518 --> 00:53:13.679
He is getting better.

00:53:13.739 --> 00:53:17.280
And he is beginning to think about love.

00:53:17.341 --> 00:53:19.422
He thinks...

00:53:19.482 --> 00:53:21.882
I love Estella.

00:53:21.942 --> 00:53:25.784
But she is cruel and she has no heart.

00:53:25.844 --> 00:53:28.596
Biddy is a very good person.

00:53:28.656 --> 00:53:30.978
She loves me.

00:53:31.038 --> 00:53:35.782
Pip wants to ask Biddy to marry him.

00:53:35.842 --> 00:53:40.436
But there is something he does not know.

00:53:40.496 --> 00:53:43.147
Biddy, I want to...

00:53:43.207 --> 00:53:44.078
Pip!

00:53:44.138 --> 00:53:46.570
I have some wonderful news.

00:53:46.630 --> 00:53:50.083
Joe and I are getting married today.

00:53:50.103 --> 00:53:51.470
But...

00:53:51.530 --> 00:53:55.980
Well, that is wonderful news.

00:53:56.040 --> 00:53:58.272
You are my best friends.

00:53:58.332 --> 00:54:00.204
I am very happy.

00:54:00.264 --> 00:54:05.249
Let me kiss you both.

00:54:05.309 --> 00:54:10.083
Part 10.

00:54:10.144 --> 00:54:12.555
Estella.

00:54:12.615 --> 00:54:17.930
So Pip begins to think about Estella again.

00:54:17.990 --> 00:54:20.664
There is news from London.

00:54:20.724 --> 00:54:24.857
Bentley Drummel is a very bad husband.

00:54:24.917 --> 00:54:27.228
He hits Estella.

00:54:27.288 --> 00:54:29.808
She never goes out.

00:54:29.868 --> 00:54:34.079
People say that she is very unhappy.

00:54:34.139 --> 00:54:36.030
Poor Estella.

00:54:36.090 --> 00:54:38.840
She's learning to have a heart.

00:54:38.900 --> 00:54:41.941
You're a very sad Pip.

00:54:42.001 --> 00:54:44.442
Can we help you?

00:54:44.502 --> 00:54:46.962
No, my friends.

00:54:47.022 --> 00:54:49.570
I must leave England.

00:54:49.630 --> 00:54:53.338
I want to go to Africa or Australia.

00:54:53.398 --> 00:54:57.800
I want to work hard and forget my problems.

00:54:57.860 --> 00:55:00.831
Pip leaves England.

00:55:00.891 --> 00:55:07.134
He works hard in the East and tries to forget everything in the past.

00:55:07.194 --> 00:55:11.575
After 11 years, he comes back.

00:55:11.635 --> 00:55:16.006
He visits Joe and Biddy and their child.

00:55:16.067 --> 00:55:20.689
Their son's name is Little Pip.

00:55:20.749 --> 00:55:26.502
Pip decides to visit Satis' house for the last time.

00:55:26.562 --> 00:55:29.574
Miss Havisham is dead.

00:55:29.634 --> 00:55:32.596
The house is not there.

00:55:32.656 --> 00:55:34.846
Only ruins.

00:55:34.906 --> 00:55:38.078
He walks in the garden.

00:55:38.138 --> 00:55:40.590
Here is the garden.

00:55:40.650 --> 00:55:43.542
I remember when I was a boy here.

00:55:43.602 --> 00:55:46.663
Estella was a beautiful little girl.

00:55:46.723 --> 00:55:50.332
And I was a poor boy from the blacksmith's family.

00:55:50.392 --> 00:55:52.440
I remember the house.

00:55:52.500 --> 00:55:55.482
I remember the clocks.

00:55:55.542 --> 00:55:57.754
But wait.

00:55:57.814 --> 00:56:00.236
There is someone in the garden.

00:56:00.296 --> 00:56:02.487
I can see a woman.

00:56:02.548 --> 00:56:05.770
She is coming towards me through the mist.

00:56:05.830 --> 00:56:07.992
Who is it?

00:56:08.052 --> 00:56:14.636
Estella comes out of the mist and meets Pip in the garden.

00:56:14.696 --> 00:56:20.226
She is still very beautiful, but her face is sad.

00:56:20.286 --> 00:56:23.971
Estella, why are you here?

00:56:24.031 --> 00:56:26.832
Bentley Drummel is dead.

00:56:26.892 --> 00:56:30.332
There was an accident with his horse.

00:56:30.392 --> 00:56:35.494
I am here to say goodbye to Satis House.

00:56:35.554 --> 00:56:38.924
And do you have a heart now?

00:56:38.984 --> 00:56:40.565
Yes, Pip.

00:56:40.625 --> 00:56:42.675
I have a heart.

00:56:42.735 --> 00:56:45.846
But it is too late.

00:56:45.906 --> 00:56:50.791
Pip is very happy to see Estella again.

00:56:50.851 --> 00:56:54.607
They talk for a long time in the garden.

00:56:54.668 --> 00:56:56.808
They hold hands.

00:56:56.868 --> 00:56:59.780
They are not young and free.

00:56:59.841 --> 00:57:02.282
They have a lot of problems.

00:57:02.342 --> 00:57:05.645
But they go out of the garden together.

00:57:05.705 --> 00:57:08.507
We are friends, Estella.

00:57:08.567 --> 00:57:12.570
We must be friends apart, Pip.

00:57:12.630 --> 00:57:17.023
Pip knows the meaning of his life.

00:57:17.083 --> 00:57:20.080
Money is not important.

00:57:20.140 --> 00:57:23.976
Being a gentleman is not important.

00:57:24.036 --> 00:57:28.951
Great expectations are not important.

00:57:29.011 --> 00:57:32.994
Friendship is important.

00:57:33.054 --> 00:57:36.358
He is friends with a stellar.

00:57:36.418 --> 00:57:38.549
They are together.

00:57:38.609 --> 00:57:45.673
There is no shadow of goodbye.

00:57:45.733 --> 00:57:49.884
Music.

